package Patterns;

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Q21 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Please enter no: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        for (int i = 0; i < n ; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <n ; j++) {
                if(i==0||j==0 || i==n-1 ||j==n-1){
                    System.out.print("*");
                }else{
                    System.out.print(" ");
                }


            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}

Approach

The pattern consists of an n × n grid where stars (*) are printed only on the border, while the inner cells remain empty.

Observation

Using nested loops:

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {     
    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) { 
i represents the row number.
j represents the column number.

A cell belongs to the border if it lies on:

Top Row    → i == 0
Bottom Row → i == n - 1
Left Col   → j == 0
Right Col  → j == n - 1

Therefore, print * whenever:

i == 0 || i == n - 1 || j == 0 || j == n - 1

Otherwise, print a space.

Logic
Traverse every cell of the n × n grid.
Check whether the current cell lies on the border.
If it is a border cell, print *.
Otherwise, print a space.
After completing one row, move to the next line.
